{"id": "L17", "command": "submit", "inputs": {"recommendation": {"decision": "switch", "challenger": "ridge_mk", "diagnosis": "The champion's error has been falling, but it still under-forecasts margins in MX and does worst late in the week, which points to markup information it cannot use. A ridge model on the markup features captures that signal and beats the champion in every corridor, while calendar and lagged-residual features add nothing on top of markup.", "evidence": [{"claim": "The champion's error over the last 26 weeks was 46.67 bps vs 67.6 bps before (-30.96%), with a positive MX bias of 5.37 bps.", "ledger_ids": ["L02", "L03"]}, {"claim": "In development, ridge on markup features scored 43.08 bps vs the champion's 46.67 bps (-7.69%), better in all three corridors: MX 43.71 bps vs 47.68 bps, IN 24.01 bps vs 27.31 bps, BR 61.43 bps vs 64.92 bps.", "ledger_ids": ["L10"]}, {"claim": "Calendar features alone gave no improvement (46.86 bps, +0.41%), and adding calendar to markup was worse (43.44 bps) than markup alone, so the gain comes from the markup features.", "ledger_ids": ["L11", "L08", "L10"]}, {"claim": "Tuning alpha did not help: the tuned config backtested at 43.12 bps (-7.61%), so the simpler untuned config was promoted.", "ledger_ids": ["L14", "L15"]}, {"claim": "The promotion test passed: the challenger scored 43.77 bps vs the champion's 46.71 bps (-6.29%), DM p-value 0.042, breach rate 0.05 vs the champion's 0.087.", "ledger_ids": ["L16"]}], "risks": "The challenger over-forecasts margins in MX and BR, so a drop in markups could hurt it. Its development gain is concentrated in a few summer months rather than spread evenly, and the worst errors are still large BR spikes that no candidate fixes.", "watch_next_week": "Watch the new model's bias in MX and BR, whether its error stays below the old champion's in each corridor, and the BR markup level, which has been falling."}}, "result": {"accepted": true, "errors": [], "attempt": 1}, "time": "2026-11-15T13:48:39Z"}
